# The payserver-client image this payserver deploys and tests against.
#
# The frontend lives in its own repository (randomcash/payserver-client) and
# publishes its own image, so it no longer shares this repo's commit sha. This
# file is the pin that replaces that coupling: an exact, immutable tag, moved
# deliberately, reviewed like any other change.
#
# Do NOT point this at `latest`. The whole reason the per-commit tag exists is
# that a moving tag makes "which frontend is live" unanswerable and a rollback
# a rebuild. The same argument that produced RCS-190 for the server images
# applies here, more so now that the frontend can change without this repo
# moving at all.
#
# To move it: pick a tag from
#   https://github.com/randomcash/payserver-client/pkgs/container/payserver-client
# and open a PR. CI pulls exactly this image for the E2E run, so a frontend that
# breaks the payment flow fails here rather than on testnet.
ghcr.io/randomcash/payserver-client:sha-1593505
